{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536581-any-spell-casting-calculators-available-2e","id":1536581,"title":"Any Spell Casting Calculators Available? (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-30T13:23:29-07:00","id":1536581,"title":"Any Spell Casting Calculators Available? (2E)","content":"I've been running an Awakening 2nd Edition game for almost a year now with a group that had never played before using Roll20. As you can imagine, casting spells has been a learning process, but thankfully there was a nifty website that had a very helpful Spell Calculator that we relied on to both learn and speed up this process.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, that website has gone down and while we're able to do it by the book, it has definitely slowed the pace of our game so I'd love to find a similar solution! All I've managed to find so far was an Android app that doesn't work on my phone. As far as I'm aware, Roll20 doesn't have any resources like this, so any suggestions would be great! I'm aware that some other virtual tabletops have this capability, but I'd like to avoid paying and transferring everything over if possible.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12268-touchofdivine","name":"TouchofDivine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T14:29:55-07:00","id":1536585,"title":"","content":"I didn't see that site went down. Interesting that nobody mentioned it.<br /> <br /> For this I have 3 suggestions<br /> <br /> 1) the book lists down&amp;dirty spellcasting rules for when appropriate.<br /> <br /> 2) don't roll dice unless you need to, if they have no time pressure (so failing means they will just try again) I would be playing fast and loose with the dice pools - just focus on practice and purview.<br /> <br /> 3) prepare spell dice pools in advance.<br /> Have people put together their spell while others are roleplaying. Ideally most of it should be background stuff.<br /> <br /> If you go 'i want to cast a death spell, I have these yantras giving me a (gnosis+Arcana+yantras bonus) dice pool / 2 worth of spell factors.<br /> <br /> Assign them, and you have however many dice are left to actually roll.<br /> <br /> If figuring out yantras is a big part, get some specific ones written down, with the pros and cons (like Runes pro: +2 yantra bonus, can be used with most any spell, cons: must be inscribed on the subject, takes [gnosis derived] ritual time to inscribe, spell ends if rune is broken) so you have a short hand for the common yantras they are using.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T13:29:30-07:00","id":1536710,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12268-touchofdivine\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12268\" data-vbnamecard=\"12268\">TouchofDivine</a> My group plays on Roll20 too, so I just wrote one. It's essentially a character sheet too, so you can setup your magical tools and calculate mudras or whatever. Keeps tabs on active spells, you can save casting setups, grimoires, copy a spell into Roll20 macro format, etc. Has export to PDF/JSON for the storyteller's benefit. It's very much for our own personal use-case, but you might find it useful.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://winstromming.github.io/spell/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://winstromming.github.io/spell/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://winstromming.github.io/spell/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://winstromming.github.io/spell/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27747-castalot","user":"Castalot","date":". 06-02-2024, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27747-castalot","name":"Castalot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}